<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        Automation runs things at the venue for you. For example, play the winner's lighting scene when a game
        ends, start a projection program when a game starts, or turn the music down before opening. It's
        Admin-only, on <a href="/automation">Automation</a>.
    </FluentText>

    <HelpSection Title="The engine switch">
        <FluentText>
            <strong>Engine: Enabled</strong> at the top turns all automation on or off at once. Each rule also has
            its own <strong>Enabled</strong> switch in the list.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Making a rule">
        <ol>
            <li>Select <strong>New Rule</strong> and give it a <strong>Rule Name</strong>.</li>
            <li>Choose the <strong>Trigger Client</strong>: the kiosk whose game it watches.</li>
            <li>Choose the <strong>Trigger Type</strong> (see below).</li>
            <li>Optionally add conditions under <strong>Only if</strong>.</li>
            <li>Add one or more actions. At least one is required.</li>
        </ol>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Trigger types">
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Game Status Change</strong>: when the kiosk's game goes <strong>In Game</strong> or <strong>Not Started</strong>.</li>
            <li><strong>Client Idle</strong>: when the kiosk has stayed at the same game status for <strong>Idle for (minutes)</strong>.</li>
            <li><strong>Scheduled</strong>: at a time of day (UK time) on the days you tick, or every day if you tick none.</li>
            <li><strong>Time remaining drops below</strong>: once per game, when the countdown passes that many seconds.</li>
            <li><strong>Score reaches</strong>: once per game, when any one player's score or a team's total reaches a value.</li>
            <li><strong>Game ends with a winner</strong>: when a team game ends with one team ahead. A draw or a game
                without teams doesn't count. Make one rule per team to give each its own scene.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
